problem_statement:
URLParam returns empty string for all parameters

#### Description

When trying to access URL parameters using `URLParam()`, the function returns an empty string for all parameters instead of the actual parameter values.

#### Steps/Code to Reproduce

```go
package main

import (
    "fmt"
    "net/http"

    "github.com/go-chi/chi/v5"
)

func main() {
    r := chi.NewRouter()

    r.Get("/users/{userID}/posts/{postID}", func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
        userID := chi.URLParam(r, "userID")
        postID := chi.URLParam(r, "postID")

        fmt.Printf("userID: %s\n", userID)
        fmt.Printf("postID: %s\n", postID)

        // Expected: userID: 123, postID: 456
        // Actual: userID: , postID: 
    })

    http.ListenAndServe(":8080", r)
}
```

When making a request to `/users/123/posts/456`, both `userID` and `postID` are empty strings instead of "123" and "456" respectively.

