problem_statement:
StatementBuilder RunWith method not working with non-nil runners

When using StatementBuilder's RunWith method with a valid database connection or transaction, the runner is being set to nil instead of the provided runner, causing queries to fail with "cannot run; no Runner set (RunWith)" error.

#### Steps to Reproduce

```go
package main

import (
    "database/sql"
    "fmt"

    "github.com/Masterminds/squirrel"
    _ "github.com/lib/pq"
)

func main() {
    db, err := sql.Open("postgres", "your-connection-string")
    if err != nil {
        panic(err)
    }
    defer db.Close()

    // This should work but fails
    stmt := squirrel.StatementBuilder.RunWith(db)
    query := stmt.Select("*").From("users").Where("id = ?", 1)

    rows, err := query.Query()
    if err != nil {
        fmt.Printf("Error: %v\n", err) // Prints: cannot run; no Runner set (RunWith)
    }
}
```

The issue occurs when trying to use any valid runner (database connection, transaction, etc.) with the StatementBuilder. The runner gets incorrectly set to nil, making it impossible to execute queries.

