problem_statement:
Hash collision handling returns wrong entry data

When a hash collision is detected in the cache, the wrong entry data is being returned instead of properly handling the collision case.

#### Steps to Reproduce

```go
package main

import (
    "fmt"
    "github.com/allegro/bigcache/v3"
    "time"
)

func main() {
    cache, _ := bigcache.NewBigCache(bigcache.DefaultConfig(10 * time.Minute))

    // These keys will have hash collision in the test hasher
    cache.Set("a", []byte("1"))
    cache.Set("b", []byte("2"))

    // This should return "1" but returns "2" due to collision handling bug
    value, err := cache.Get("a")
    if err != nil {
        fmt.Printf("Error: %v\n", err)
    } else {
        fmt.Printf("Expected: 1, Got: %s\n", string(value))
    }
}
```

The issue occurs when two different keys hash to the same value. Instead of returning an error or the correct entry for the requested key, the cache returns the colliding entry's data.

