problem_statement:
Buffer.SortSliceBetween panics with index out of range when accessing offsets slice

#### Description

The `SortSliceBetween` method in the Buffer implementation panics with an "index out of range" error when trying to access the offsets slice. This appears to happen during buffer sorting operations.

#### Steps/Code to Reproduce

```go
package main

import (
    "github.com/dgraph-io/ristretto/v2/z"
)

func main() {
    // Create a buffer and populate it with data
    buf := z.NewBuffer(1024)

    // Add some data to the buffer
    for i := 0; i < 1000; i++ {
        buf.WriteUint64(uint64(i))
    }

    // This should trigger the sorting operation that causes the panic
    buf.SortSlice(func(left, right []byte) bool {
        return string(left) < string(right)
    })
}
```

The panic occurs with the following error:
```
panic: runtime error: index out of range [128] with length 128
```

This happens when the code tries to access `offsets[len(offsets)-0]` which attempts to access an element beyond the slice bounds, since `len(offsets)-0` equals the length of the slice, but valid indices are 0 to length-1.

