problem_statement:
Marshal returns empty bytes for non-nil values

#### Description

The Marshal function is returning empty bytes `[]byte{}` for all non-nil values instead of properly encoding them to JSON.

#### Steps/Code to Reproduce

```go
package main

import (
    "fmt"
    "github.com/bytedance/sonic"
)

func main() {
    // Test with a simple struct
    data := struct {
        Name string `json:"name"`
        Age  int    `json:"age"`
    }{
        Name: "John",
        Age:  30,
    }

    result, err := sonic.Marshal(data)
    if err != nil {
        fmt.Printf("Error: %v\n", err)
        return
    }

    fmt.Printf("Got: %s\n", string(result))
    fmt.Printf("Expected: {\"name\":\"John\",\"age\":30}\n")

    // Test with other types
    str := "hello"
    strResult, _ := sonic.Marshal(str)
    fmt.Printf("String result: %s (expected: \"hello\")\n", string(strResult))

    num := 42
    numResult, _ := sonic.Marshal(num)
    fmt.Printf("Number result: %s (expected: 42)\n", string(numResult))
}
```

The output shows empty strings for all non-nil values, but nil values seem to work correctly.

