problem_statement:
Reverse bitmap iterator returns incorrect results for empty containers

#### Description

When iterating in reverse over an empty bitmap container, the iterator incorrectly initializes and may return unexpected values instead of properly handling the empty case.

#### Steps/Code to Reproduce

```go
package main

import (
    "fmt"
    "github.com/RoaringBitmap/roaring/v2"
)

func main() {
    // Create an empty bitmap
    rb := roaring.NewBitmap()

    // Try to iterate in reverse - should return no values
    it := rb.ReverseIterator()

    fmt.Println("Iterating over empty bitmap in reverse:")
